  "units": "Native 690px-wide JPEG, top-left pixel coordinates. Positive X is image-right, and positive model Y runs into the gate.",
  "read_method": "Original photo crops were straightened along the top of the three rows. Egg centres were read in X, with the visible middle of the row estimated from its local slope. Native-image controls were frozen before first-hit testing. The changing illumination and chipped left boundary limit exact centre identification. The six lags below are from horizontal row-wise image autocorrelation after a 3-pixel Gaussian high pass.",
  "scope": "The two framings show a central recessed bed and two projecting heads. Thirteen full eggs can be followed through the central storey. Six fit the right bed. Five fit the left head up to its weathered outside edge. One egg on each short inner return is a bounded reconstruction; the underside, rear surfaces, and return relief are less directly visible. Depth follows the adopted portal camera family, with no independently surveyed absolute scale.",
